  "notes": "Atlanta’s sample-and-sound-effect melodist for the Thug/Migos axis. His signature move is documented and unusual: **found sound as the lead melody** — the research’s example is a bat hitting a pole used as the lead — set against \"hard, trap drums\" he treats as the identity of the record. Harmony is 70s soul transplanted into trap, so the sample supplies the motion and the 808 stays root-locked underneath rather than riffing. ⚠ `medium`: DAW, hardware, sampling sources and the foley habit are documented; the research rates it high-medium.",
